[signal arg="CONVOSTART"]
set {ClaudEnlighten} = false
Claudma: Hello, Virtue.
- Are you my client?
	Claudma: Careful with whom you speak, Virtue
	Claudma: We are Claudma
	Claudma: With us begins motion
	Claudma: With us ends spirit
	Claudma: ..and by us it repeats
	Virtue: (I think they want me to speak)
	- The contract
		Virtue: Im here to discuss our contract...
		Virtue: You want me to be the defence attorney of humanity?
		Claudma: As it is in your presence here, yes.
		Claudma: It was of our will that we summoned your services.
		Claudma: However, it is really you that is accused.
		Virtue: how so?
		Claudma: It is you who will convince us, the council, why humanity should exist.
		Virtue: ...
		Virtue: I've took on harder cases.
		Virtue: Although I cant say this isnt a bit unorthodox.
		Virtue: If'n any other case I spoke to the prosecutor before a trial I'd be disbarred immediatley. Odd rules you people play by.
		if {ChToCla} == true:
			- [Lovley mist]
				Virtue: The man out front... uh, the one with antlers? he wants you to know the mist is lovley outside.
				Claudma: You've spoken with the man of bones?
				Claudma: That is a troubled one. For this remark we shall enlighten you.
				Claudma: Authority and chaos are bound by dreams.
				Claudma: Without dreams, spirits will have no hold, no handle in the world. So to understand what it means to walk on ground, you must understand this basic truth.
				Claudma: Your mortality is not linear. when truths lie behind your eyes, do not claim to know it.
				set {ClaudEnlighten} = true
				jump DialogueBody
		else:
			label DialogueBody
			- What are your thoughts on humanity?
				Virtue: As stated in the contract, the defendant is accused of various, as it was put, "profane crimes against existence"
				Virtue: before moving to court with this, do you have any comments related to these allegations?
				Claudma: For what little time man has walked, they have stepped upon the worlds of many
				Claudma: With each footprint, worlds destroyed. Cries of a thousand lives. Thousands of civilizations extinguished like that of a candle.
				Claudma: Of all humans that walk none speak of the sanctity of ground. Not dirt, but ground. The spirits that lie beneath the quilts of fabric upon which existence predicates itself
				Claudma: I do not desire to make humanity one of these extinguished lives. However, you must first understand what it means to walk on ground before you can convince the other timeless ones.
				jump DialogueBody
			- Im the best there is
				Virtue: As far as criminal defence attorneys go, I can assure you. You've hired the best.
				Claudma: May that be known in due time.
				Claudma: But let not this heir of hubris possess you. For you walk among endless ones.
				jump DialogueBody
			- (Exit Conversation)
				set {ClaudmaInteract} = false
				[signal arg="CONVOISOVER"]
				[end_timeline]